{{Quote|There is no map to At Attin. No, this scroll depicts the Jewels of the Old Republic. Planets of wonder kept hidden for their protection.|Kh'ymm|<ref name="Astrogation" />}}
The '''Jewels of the Old Republic''' were a group of nine [[planet]]s that were hidden long before the [[New Republic Era]]. Most of the planets were at some point believed destroyed, with only [[At Attin]] said to be remaining.<ref name="Astrogation" /> Over time, At Attin acquired legendary status as the "lost planet of eternal treasure" among citizens of [[the galaxy]],<ref name="Way, Way Out Past the Barrier">{{SkeletonCrew|Way, Way Out Past the Barrier}}</ref> whereas the citizens of At Attin remained ignorant to the galaxy at large, committing themselves to the [[Great Work]] of the [[Galactic Republic]] many years after the [[Proclamation of the New Order|fall]] of that incarnation of the Republic.<ref name="This Could Be a Real Adventure">{{SkeletonCrew|This Could Be a Real Adventure}}</ref> 

Another one of the Jewels, [[At Achrann]], was a war-torn world that greatly resembled At Attin, with two tribes&mdash;the [[Troik]] and [[Hattan]]&mdash;fighting each other in the era of the New Republic. Four of the other Jewels were [[At Aytuu]], [[At Aravin]], [[At Arissia]], and [[At Acoda]].<ref name="Can't Say" />

